.gm/long-gap-retry-state
# gm rewrites this digest/count marker as it exports memories, so a tracked copy dirties the
# worktree on every chain and blocks the COMPLETE gate for no reason. Same class as the runtime
# state already listed above.
.gm/memories/.flat-export-done
# gm-continue's own recursion counter. Its docs say it is "reset by a fresh user prompt", so it is
# rewritten on essentially every session and every re-invocation -- tracked, that dirties the
# worktree and blocks the COMPLETE gate for a file no human edits. Same class as the marker above.
.gm/.gm-continue-count
.gm/turn-state.json
.gm/mutables.yml
.gm/prd.yml
.gm/next-step.md
.gm/instructions/
.gm/residual-check-fired
.gm/claim-audit-fired
.gm/.instructions-shipped-manifest.json
# agentplug's own local key-value cache, root-anchored (holoiroh/.agentplug-kv/ above covers a
# different, nested location) -- rewritten on essentially every gm dispatch, same runtime-state
# class as the exec-spool/rs-learn.db entries above.
.agentplug-kv/
# gm's own embed-model-version marker, rewritten whenever the code-index embed generation
# changes -- same class as .gm-continue-count above (no human edits this file).
# The wildcard also covers the per-scope markers (.embed-generation.code_chunks and
# similar) that the current runner writes beside the base marker.
.gm/.embed-generation*
# The agentplug runner's machine checkout and its per-project dispatch cache at the
# repo root. Tooling state, not source. The nested holoiroh copy is covered below.
agentplug/
.agentplug/
.claude/
.turbo/
coverage/
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
*.patch
holoiroh/ios/Artifacts/
holoiroh/ios-app/HoloIroh.xcodeproj/
# xcodebuild -derivedDataPath output from device deploys (regenerable, ~GBs).
holoiroh/ios-app/build/
# same xcodebuild -derivedDataPath output, for the newer ios/App/ scaffolding.
holoiroh/ios/App/build/
# holoiroh's own gm/agentplug session state (same rationale as the root .gm/
# ignores above -- volatile orchestrator state, never source).
holoiroh/.gm/
holoiroh/.agentplug-kv/
holoiroh/.agentplug/
# Unrelated local exercises living inside the holoiroh tree; excluded from the
# cargo workspace (see holoiroh/Cargo.toml) and from version control alike.
holoiroh/rust_db_project/
holoiroh/hello_world/

# gm runtime state can appear under ANY directory a watcher was booted from,
# not just the repo root -- the rules above are root-anchored, so a stray boot
# from a subdirectory (e.g. holoiroh/mac-daemon/) left a live heartbeat file
# tracked and churning in commits. These patterns match at any depth.
**/.gm/exec-spool/
**/.gm/witness/
**/.gm/browser-state/
**/.gm/rs-learn.db
**/.gm/gm.db

# Cloned working copy of the remote gm config repo plus its sync marker, both
# fetched at runtime and re-created on demand -- committing a nested checkout
# would embed another repo's history in this one.
**/.gm/config-source-cache*/
**/.gm/config-source-cache*.sync.json
